{#
  module/Books/view/books/publications/publication-info.phtml, ported — the
  bibliographic panel that is most of a publication page.

  Expects:
    object            the publication row
    cover_url         the full-size cover URL, or null when no cover file exists on disk
    cover_thumb_url   the 400px cover URL, or null
    edit_url          where the "Edit publication" button goes
    merged_into_url   the surviving edition's URL, or null when this row is not merged
    copy_to_corpus_url  the "Copy into main corpus" URL, or null
    other_editions    subEditions + translations, merged, as the original does

  Everything that needed the filesystem, the router or an identifier filter is resolved
  in App\Controller\PublicationController and arrives as a variable — `file_exists()`
  against `public/covers/…` most of all, which a template has no business doing.

  The original also takes an `options` array with `showCover` and a `panelTitle` of
  `book-title-and-link`, which swaps the "Publication Info" heading for the formatted
  publication itself.

  **This block said "nothing passes either" and that was true only until batch 11b.**
  `books/books/show.phtml` renders this partial with *both* — `showCover: false` and
  `panelTitle: 'book-title-and-link'` — so a book page shows the publication panel
  headed by a link to the publication rather than by the words "Publication Info". The
  branch was dropped when this file was written on the reasoning that it was
  unreachable, which was a statement about the four routes ported at the time and read
  as a statement about the application. Restored 2026-08-18, and the lesson is worth
  more than the branch: "nothing calls this" is only ever true of the code that exists
  when you write it down.

  ## The four FormatPublication display modes

  This partial is the reason App\Laminas\EntityFormatter grew them. It uses `authors`
  for the author line, `edition` beside each other edition, `disambiguatingTitle` for the
  current publication, `translators` for the translator line, and the default `title`
  everywhere else. Each of the three list modes renders **without** a link, a pencil or
  status icons, because the original defaults all five of those options to the title
  modes — see that class.

  ## Two permission checks that are not the route guard

  `isAllowed(resourceId, 'edit')` gates the edit button and
  `isAllowed(resourceId, 'show-admin-info')` gates the admin-notes panel — both against
  the publication's *own* ACL resource, not the route. A publication in the institute
  corpus therefore shows its edit button to a different set of people than a public one
  does, on the same page, and neither has anything to do with reaching the page at all.
  `format_field`'s `displayOnlyWithPermission` is a third such check, inside the helper.
#}
{% import 'schoenstatt/_entity-format.html.twig' as format %}
{% set show_cover = show_cover|default(true) %}
<div class="row">
{% if show_cover %}
<div class="col-md-3">
    {% if cover_thumb_url is not null %}
        <a href="{{ cover_url }}">
        <img src="{{ cover_thumb_url }}"
        class="img-responsive center-block" alt="{{ object.title }}"></a>
    {% endif %}
<p class="align-center"></p>
</div>
{% endif %}
<div class="col-md-{{ show_cover ? 9 : 12 }}">
<div class="panel panel-default" id="infoPanel">
    <div class="panel-heading">
        <div class="row">
        <div class="col-xs-6">
            <h3 class="panel-title">{% if panel_title|default('text') == 'book-title-and-link' %}{{ format.entity('publication', object) }}{% else %}{{ translate('Publication Info') }}{% endif %}</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="col-xs-6">
            {% if is_allowed(object.resourceId, 'edit') %}
                <span class="pull-right"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" href="{{ edit_url }}">
                    {{ translate('Edit publication') }}</a>
                </span>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-body"><div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-6">
          <p><strong>{{ translate('Author(s)') }}:</strong></p>
            {{ format_entity('publication', object, {'display': 'authors'}) }}
{% if other_editions is not empty %}
      <p><strong>{{ translate('Other editions') }}:</strong></p>
{% for sub in other_editions %}
          <p>{{ format_entity('publication', sub) }} {{ format_entity('publication', sub, {'display': 'edition'}) }}</p>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
    </div> <!-- info 1 column -->

    <div class="col-md-6">
        <p><strong>{{ translate('Language') }}:</strong> {% if object.inLanguage is not empty %}{% for language in object.inLanguage %}{{ language_name(language) }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}</p>
        {% if object.mainPublication is not null %}
        <p><strong>{{ translate('Current publication') }}:</strong> {{ format_entity('publication', object.mainPublication, {'display': 'disambiguatingTitle'}) }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        {% if object.translatedFromPublication is not null %}
        <p><strong>{{ translate('Translated from') }}:</strong> {{ format_entity('publication', object.translatedFromPublication) }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        {{ format_field('ISBN', object.isbn, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Edition', object.bookEdition, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {% if object.translatorsAll is not empty %}
        <p><strong>{{ translate('Translator(s)') }}</strong>: {{ format_entity('publication', object, {'display': 'translators'}) }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        {{ format_field('Number of pages', object.numberOfPages, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Date published', object.datePublishedText, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Publisher', object.publisher, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Publishing place', object.publishingPlace, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Copyright year', object.copyrightYear, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Book format', object.bookFormatType, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Volume number', object.volumeNumber, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Contained in', object.containedIn, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Contained in ISBN', object.containedInIsbn, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Genre', object.genre, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Keywords', object.keywords, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true, 'translateLabel': false}) }}
        {{ format_field('Admin tags', object.adminTags, {
            'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true,
            'translateLabel': false,
            'displayOnlyWithPermission': 'route/publication-edit',
        }) }}
{#- the <hr> depends on all three, so it stays a single test rather than three -#}
{% if object.dataSource is not null or object.dataSourceId is not null or object.mergedIntoPublicationId is not null %}<hr>{% endif %}
        {{ format_field('Data source', object.dataSource, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
        {{ format_field('Original ID within data source', object.dataSourceId, {'displayOnlyIfNotNull': true}) }}
{% if merged_into_url is not null %}
            <p><strong>{{ translate('Merged into') }}</strong>:
                <a href="{{ merged_into_url }}">
                    {{ object.mergedIntoPublicationId }}</a>
            </p>
{% elseif copy_to_corpus_url is not null %}
            <p><a href="{{ copy_to_corpus_url }}" class="btn btn-default">
                {{ translate('Copy into main corpus') }}
            </a></p>
{% endif %}
{% for url_object in object.urls %}
<p>{{ publication_url_object(url_object) }}</p>
{% endfor %}
    </div> <!-- info 2 column -->
    </div></div> <!-- contact info panel body -->
</div> <!-- info 1 panel -->
</div> <!-- info 1 column -->
</div> <!-- Info row -->

{% if object.publicNotes is not empty %}
<div class="row"> <!-- notes row -->
<div class="col-md-12">
<div class="panel panel-default" id="notesPanel">
    <div class="panel-heading">
        <h3 class="panel-title">{{ translate('Notes') }}</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-body">
    <div>{{ markdown(object.publicNotes) }}
    </div>
    </div> <!-- notes panel body -->
</div> <!-- notes panel -->
</div> <!-- notes column 12 -->
</div> <!-- notes row -->
{% endif %}

{% if object.adminNotes is not empty and is_allowed(object.resourceId, 'show-admin-info') %}
<div class="row"> <!-- notes row -->
<div class="col-md-12">
<div class="panel panel-default" id="adminNotesPanel">
    <div class="panel-heading">
        <h3 class="panel-title">{{ translate('Admin notes') }}</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-body">
    <div>{{ markdown(object.adminNotes) }}
    </div>
    </div> <!-- notes panel body -->
</div> <!-- notes panel -->
</div> <!-- notes column 12 -->
</div> <!-- notes row -->
{% endif %}

{{ books_json_ld('publication', object) }}
{{ coins('publication', object) }}
